import H0mework.Versions.Re60a8605.ReleaseMaterials.SaturationMonoid.ProcessGame.Regression.Society.M14.Fixture.Economy.Credit.Risk.Merge.Capacity.Runtime.Payment.Novelty.PostSettlement.Representation.Failure.SourceGeneratedContributionCapacityFinitePrefixRepresentationBreaking
import H0mework.Versions.Re60a8605.ReleaseMaterials.SaturationMonoid.ProcessGame.Regression.Society.M14.Fixture.Economy.Credit.Risk.Merge.Capacity.Renewal.Settlement.Joint.Renewal.Submission.Action.Transport.Consumer.ProofCarryingPostSettlementObserverSubmissionExternalPaymentLegislation

/-!
# Finite-prefix representation breaking transported to the existing Q self-U8

The P-side breaking is source-native and keeps its ordinary paid successor.
The same right replay also generates the distinct external Q Payment.  This
file transports the two empty operational extension fibres to the already
installed M9 failure fibres, then consumes the existing rooted failure,
minimal coface, runtime, first write and reflexive self-U8.

No action program, target root, revised core, next selector or future schedule
is introduced.  P and Q remain distinct ambient occurrences with separate
authority.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace ProcessGame
namespace Society
namespace M14SourceGeneratedContributionCapacityFinitePrefixRepresentationBreakingU8Transport

noncomputable section

open ResponsibilityLifecycle LivingLawEvolution ConstructiveRoot
open ConstructiveRoot.RootInquiryCompletion
open ConstructiveRoot.ObstructionGeneratedMinimalCoface
open Renewal Legislation Theory.Revision
open Society.Revision
